# Azure DevOps CI/CD Learning Notes

## Overview

Today, I learned the fundamentals of **CI/CD (Continuous Integration and Continuous Delivery/Deployment)** using **Azure DevOps**. The session covered the CI/CD workflow, Azure DevOps services, pipeline components, advantages of automation, and software deployment process.

---

## Topics Covered

### Continuous Integration (CI)
- Introduction to CI
- Automated code integration
- Build automation
- Automated testing
- Build artifact generation

### Continuous Delivery (CD)
- Deployment to Development, Testing, UAT, and Production
- Manual approval before production deployment

### Continuous Deployment
- Fully automated deployment to production
- Continuous software delivery

### Azure DevOps Services
- Azure Repos
- Azure Pipelines
- Azure Boards
- Azure Test Plans
- Azure Artifacts

### Azure Pipeline Components
- Pipeline
- Agent
- Stage
- Job
- Task
- Artifact

### Advantages of CI/CD
- Faster software delivery
- Improved code quality
- Automated testing
- Early bug detection
- Reduced manual effort
- Consistent deployments
- Better collaboration
- Increased productivity

### CI/CD Workflow
- Code Commit
- Build
- Test
- Package
- Deploy to Development
- Deploy to Testing
- Deploy to UAT
- Deploy to Production

---

## Learning Outcome
Gained a clear understanding of CI/CD concepts, Azure DevOps services, pipeline components, deployment workflow, and the benefits of automating software build, testing, and deployment processes.

